(5728949, 832565, 96530, '<td valign="top">Thanks CJ, I was hoping this one would do a little better too but with so little feedback I can only guess why it didn''t. Was the wide angle distortion considered weird instead of unique? Did the colors look cooked even though they aren''t? Maybe it''s the leaves moving in the wind with the long exposure made people feel it was out of focus?  Maybe I was a little too "different" by taking one of the only twilight images in the gallery? I''m at a complete loss as to what I could do different next time to please more voters. Hmmmm.... could have been worse :-)</td>', 'Thanks CJ, I was hoping this one would do a little better too but with so little feedback I can only guess why it didn''t. Was the wide angle distortion considered weird instead of unique? Did the colors look cooked even though they aren''t? Maybe it''s the leaves moving in the wind with the long exposure made people feel it was out of focus?  Maybe I was a little too "different" by taking one of the only twilight images in the gallery? I''m at a complete loss as to what I could do different next time to please more voters. Hmmmm.... could have been worse :-)', '2009-11-16 12:08:23.000000', NULL, 0),
