(5733788, 831605, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very few low votes, which is good!  Nice even distribution.  One thing I''d suggest is avoiding very "stand out" kinds of borders.  Some people hate them.  I only notice borders if they call attention to themselves.  This one does a little.</td>', 'Very few low votes, which is good!  Nice even distribution.  One thing I''d suggest is avoiding very "stand out" kinds of borders.  Some people hate them.  I only notice borders if they call attention to themselves.  This one does a little.', '2009-11-19 15:35:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5733945, 830228, 81530, '<td valign="top">Cool shot David, got an 8 from me.</td>', 'Cool shot David, got an 8 from me.', '2009-11-19 17:33:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5734162, 831766, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Very soft and subdued, nicely balanced compostion.  I love to find shots too, as opposed to go and make them, which can be fun too!<br/> <br/>Technical: Hard to find fault. I''m a sucker for leading lines and ambient lighting, both of which you use well here. Deeper dof may have helped, as only the closer shoreline is in focus, but I like the impressionistic feel with a shallower dof.  Does add to the painterly feel. You don''t mention any post-processing steps, so if this is straight from the camera, well done!<br/> <br/>Artistic: At a guess, I would say it''s your lack of over-saturated colours that caused you to finish fairly low, as this site tends to favour deep saturation.  I tend to go for an extreme or different POV; try kneeling or crouching in same location and Having said that, if it''s your second challenge, then there''s no place to go but up.<br/> <br/>Overall: A lovely image, good work, keep shooting!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Very soft and subdued, nicely balanced compostion.  I love to find shots too, as opposed to go and make them, which can be fun too! Technical: Hard to find fault. I''m a sucker for leading lines and ambient lighting, both of which you use well here. Deeper dof may have helped, as only the closer shoreline is in focus, but I like the impressionistic feel with a shallower dof.  Does add to the painterly feel. You don''t mention any post-processing steps, so if this is straight from the camera, well done! Artistic: At a guess, I would say it''s your lack of over-saturated colours that caused you to finish fairly low, as this site tends to favour deep saturation.  I tend to go for an extreme or different POV; try kneeling or crouching in same location and Having said that, if it''s your second challenge, then there''s no place to go but up. Overall: A lovely image, good work, keep shooting! Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-11-19 20:05:47.000000', NULL, 0),
