(5739083, 832032, 54645, '<td valign="top">The experience is enjoyable. The comments by some are just as interesting. I still don''t know how you did this or "what I''m looking at", but I like the visual journey of exploring the photograph in relation to the title. My initial impression was of a human looking through a window but that foreground reflection (?), grime, and texture, gives the eerie feeling of being watched. The title gave that human/presence a goal. Great example of a photograph creating introspection from the subjects perspective, but the subject is dynamic, dependent on the viewer. Your comments give that introspection direction.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-11-24 00:43:22.</i></td>', 'The experience is enjoyable. The comments by some are just as interesting. I still don''t know how you did this or "what I''m looking at", but I like the visual journey of exploring the photograph in relation to the title. My initial impression was of a human looking through a window but that foreground reflection (?), grime, and texture, gives the eerie feeling of being watched. The title gave that human/presence a goal. Great example of a photograph creating introspection from the subjects perspective, but the subject is dynamic, dependent on the viewer. Your comments give that introspection direction.', '2009-11-24 00:40:42.000000', '2009-11-24 00:43:22.000000', 0),
