(5742797, 829980, 102315, '<td valign="top">I agree with the majority of coments below. <br/> <br/>There is no focal point on this image. My eyes wonder left and right, up and down. I don''t know what to stop and look at. I also think the blur on the leaves really hurt an outdoor image. I personally try to stay away from multiple shot HDR''s (especially the amount you used)in outdoor scene''s because of this reason. Sometimes they work and sometimes there is just too much movement. Just too much blur to compensate. An alternative to this may be shooting in RAW and using a single image to convert to HDR?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-11-26 12:14:13.</i></td>', 'I agree with the majority of coments below.  There is no focal point on this image. My eyes wonder left and right, up and down. I don''t know what to stop and look at. I also think the blur on the leaves really hurt an outdoor image. I personally try to stay away from multiple shot HDR''s (especially the amount you used)in outdoor scene''s because of this reason. Sometimes they work and sometimes there is just too much movement. Just too much blur to compensate. An alternative to this may be shooting in RAW and using a single image to convert to HDR?', '2009-11-26 12:12:07.000000', '2009-11-26 12:14:13.000000', 0),
(5743272, 832422, 25355, '<td valign="top">This so reminds me of my travels in England. I can imagine sound the cows mooing, sheeps baaing, birds chattering, and the smell of manure wafting through the air. ;-)<br/>  Well done in getting top ten.</td>', 'This so reminds me of my travels in England. I can imagine sound the cows mooing, sheeps baaing, birds chattering, and the smell of manure wafting through the air. ;-)  Well done in getting top ten.', '2009-11-26 21:56:07.000000', NULL, 0),
